    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d693">

                <pb facs="0904" n="808" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg808"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cambon to Mr.
                            Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >French Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-08-29"><hi rendition="#italic">August 29,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The French embassy has just received a telegram from Habana in which
                    Captain-General Blanco expresses the wish to know whether the Federal Government
                    would see any objection to officers of the Spanish army returning singly to
                    Spain by way of the United States.</p>
                <p>The French embassy would be much obliged to the Department of State if it would
                    enable it to reply to this question by telegram.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
